 where\, so it is not a fresh route. Size S is an editorial estimate.\nSco
 pe: Probabilistic and Bayesian machine learning\, emphasizing approximate
  inference\, variational and Monte Carlo methods\, Gaussian processes\, g
 raphical and state-space models\, calibration\, and decisions under uncer
 tainty. Includes Bayesian optimization and uncertainty-aware deep learnin
 g. The reviewed 2026 application focus is healthcare and climate\; probab
 ilistic reasoning remains essential to a suitable contribution.\nAddition
 al topics: Deep Representation Learning\, Reinforcement Learning\, Time S
 eries & Sequential Data\, Robustness & Safety\nScope sources (2026): http
 s://probml.cc/call/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
